{
  "id": "u08-l08",
  "unit": "u08-daily-routine",
  "title": "I can, I think",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Can** = infinitive + **পারা**, and পারা takes the person endings you know:\n\n- আমি বলতে **পারি** — I can speak\n- আপনি বলতে **পারেন** — you can speak (polite)\n- সে বলতে **পারে** — he/she can speak\n\n**বলতে** 'to speak' works like **খেতে** 'to eat' from Unit 4. For 'can't', add **না** at the end: খেতে **পারি না** 'I can't eat'. You already know the chunk **বুঝতে পারছি না** 'I don't understand' — that is the same verb.\n\nTo give an opinion, start with **(আমার) মনে হয়** 'I think' (lit. 'it comes to my mind'). **হয়তো** 'maybe' is less sure: **হয়তো সে অফিসে** 'Maybe she's at the office'.\n\nIn class: **আমার একটা প্রশ্ন আছে** 'I have a question', **উত্তর কী?** 'What's the answer?'",
